jobResponsibilities:
The jobholder is responsible for implementing and maintaining robust security measures for the safe and secure custody of residents in YH. The jobholder is to monitor the security system and ensure that they are effective in supporting SGH’s operations. The jobholder is to assist DD/OSU in conducting exercises to test YH operational readiness. This also includes ensuring exercises are also conducted across all residential blocks.
The jobholder is required to conduct investigation as directed by DD/ OSU. This encompasses conducting comprehensive investigation of all serious incidents involving both residents and staff. The jobholder is to ensure thorough, non-judgmental, fair, transparent and objective investigation into possible breaches of discipline and recommend appropriate course of disciplinary proceedings based on severity of the offence committed and valid mitigating factors.

Main Responsibilities:
1.Investigate cases as assigned and to obtain evidence such as photos, medical reports, CCTV/BWC footages, record necessary statements and to complete up the SOF with recommendation on the appropriate charge to DD/OSU for his endorsement;
2. Collate and track youth infringement records;
3. Keep track of Fire, Duress Drill and Security Items Report submitted by Youth Guidance and Management and Education Unit;
4. Work closely with appointed security vendor with regards to Preventive maintenance and Trouble Shootings in SGH and to ensure that regular checks and audits are conducted by vendor to ensure that the system is in good order;
5. Indent/booking of CISCO to escort residents (eg: Court, hospital, WPLN, other appointment) and to certify monthly payment for the work performed by APOs; and manage all APO matters.
6. Check security equipment – Walkie talkie, complex keys, handcuffs and flexi cuffs in all blocks. (quarterly);
7. Oversee the regular inspection of physical security structure and ensure that it is in good order; proper inventory of security equipment, lock-set and keys and send equipment for repair when defect is reported;
8. Manage Visitor Management System;
9.Perform screening and maintaining database for long term contractors/ vendors/visitors/ trainers; and
10. Ensure immediate remedy for any security gaps which are identified in terms of physical infrastructure and security procedures

jobRequirements:
1. Strong in written and spoken English;
2. Experience in investigation is a useful advantage;
3. Possess good interpersonal and communication skills to engage residents, and good understanding of youth culture and dynamics;
4. Ability to multi-task, work independently and be an effective team player; and
5. Possess good IT knowledge and computer-related skills e.g. Microsoft Words, Excel, Office, PowerPoint.

jobResponsibilities:
You will be involved in the following:

•	Work closely with Singapore and International Judges as well as Judicial Officers in matters affecting cases before the SICC and on appeals from the SICC;
•	Manage cases filed in or transferred from the GDHC to the SICC through analysing, reviewing, monitoring and processing documents in accordance with the applicable legislation, rules, practice directions, standard operating procedures and policies;
•	Draft case summaries, papers, notices and general correspondence and liaise with lawyers, self-represented persons and other stakeholders (including external agencies) to facilitate smooth proceedings and the efficient disposal of cases;
•	Compile, verify and maintain accurate case information and statistics, preparing reports including providing analysis of the statistics where appropriate, and recommend measures to enhance the operations of the SICC;
•	Establish, review and streamline existing operational processes to improve quality of work and productivity to meet the key performance indicators of the SICC;
•	Manage and provide support in the development and implementation of operational systems or changes thereto or in administering the operations of the SICC;
•	Conduct legal research and analysis with a view to making recommendations on issues affecting the operations of the SICC; 
•	Review and enhance rules of court, practice directions and practices, and make recommendations to address operational or system implications; and  
•	Assist in the functions and work of the Registry in general (including working with other divisions in the Supreme Court) and as assigned.

• Participate in designing and modernisation of data centre infrastructure;
• Manage data centre operations, which include formulation and assessment of KPIs, capacity planning, usage management etc;
• Coordinate with stakeholders during incident response and remediation of issues
• Manage data centre modernisation and technology upgrade projects;
• Manage data centre maintenance contracts;
• Provide technical consultancy to stakeholders regarding project on-boarding;
• Review and refine existing workflows as part of on-going digital transformation for Data Centre operation;
• Explore new technologies and solutions to improve operational efficiency and physical security of data centre.

agencyDescription:
The Ministry of Finance (MOF) is responsible for managing Singapore’s fiscal policies and the structure of its economy. We work to maintain international standards and best practices in areas such as company law, accounting standards, and corporate governance principles. We aim to advance the well-being and development of Singapore by:

•	achieving a balanced budget through prudent and sustainable fiscal policies;
•	ensuring the prudent investment of the government's reserves and other public funds;
•	setting out policies for government procurement, customs regulation, accounting standards and business regulation;
•	fostering a regulatory environment conducive to business and enterprise; and
•	ensuring that businesses operating within Singapore's jurisdiction are compatible with international standards and practices, in areas such as company law, accounting standards and corporate governance principles.

The Ministry of Finance (MOF) is responsible for managing Singapore’s fiscal policies and the structure of its economy. We work to maintain international standards and best practices in areas such as company law, accounting standards, and corporate governance principles. We aim to advance the well-being and development of Singapore by:

•	achieving a balanced budget through prudent and sustainable fiscal policies;
•	ensuring the prudent investment of the government's reserves and other public funds;
•	setting out policies for government procurement, customs regulation, accounting standards and business regulation;
•	fostering a regulatory environment conducive to business and enterprise; and
•	ensuring that businesses operating within Singapore's jurisdiction are compatible with international standards and practices, in areas such as company law, accounting standards and corporate governance principles.

jobRequirements:
•	Relevant course of study in a quantitative discipline, e.g. accountancy, engineering, mathematics, economics, finance, and/or data analytics with 2 to 5 years of relevant working experience;
•	Prior experience working in a finance/transformation/analytics-related function within the Singapore Public Service with working knowledge of related policies (e.g. Government Instruction Manuals), experience in the use of Government central financial platforms (e.g. NFS@Gov, HRPS, IBudget 2 and Fi@Gov) and/or automation/data visualisation tools (e.g. UIPath, Tableau) would be advantageous;
•	Strong analytical skills; meticulous with ability to deep-dive into processes and data;
•	Good communication and interpersonal skills to work with different internal business units and stakeholders;
•	Committed, responsible and self-driven with passion for continuous learning and improvement;
•	Ability to work independently and effectively as a team;
•	Proficient in the use of Microsoft Word, Excel and PowerPoint.

agencyDescription:
The National Research Foundation (NRF) was set up on 1 January 2006 as a department under the Prime Minister's Office. It was set up to perform the following:

a) To provide secretariat support to the Research, Innovation and Enterprise Council (RIEC), chaired by the Senior Minister;

b) To coordinate the research of different agencies within the larger national framework in order to provide a coherent strategic overview and direction;

c) To develop policies and plans to implement the five strategic thrusts for the national R&D agenda; and

d) To implement national research, innovation and enterprise strategies approved by the RIEC, and to allocate funding to programmes that meet NRF's strategic objectives.

jobResponsibilities:
(1) An AI-based knowledge management solution to improve how the division organises and retrieves its resources; 
(2) A Python-based Case Management System with a working user interface for officers to log and track cases, along with a handover guide. 

Learning outcomes: Practical experience applying AI tools, building software for end users, and working within a public service environment.

You will work as part of a team to support our international relations operations and forge partnerships with other nations and profile MCCY among international partners. The responsibilities include: 



•	Supporting MCCY's political office holders and senior management on key international relations engagements by managing courtesy calls, visits and events. You will be required to staff overseas trips; 

•	Develop and execute strategies with our internal stakeholders to expand Singapore’s international influence through cultural diplomacy; 

•	Working and coordinating with MCCY internal stakeholders to ensure alignment and support of our diplomatic agenda; 

•	Working with MFA and other SINGOV agencies to advance the interests of Singapore internationally through collaboration on international meetings / events; and 

•	Coordinating MCCY’s efforts to support Singapore’s ASEAN Chairmanship in 2027

