The Ministry of Finance (MOF) is responsible for managing Singapore’s fiscal policies and the structure of its economy. We work to maintain international standards and best practices in areas such as company law, accounting standards, and corporate governance principles. We aim to advance the well-being and development of Singapore by:

•	achieving a balanced budget through prudent and sustainable fiscal policies;
•	ensuring the prudent investment of the government's reserves and other public funds;
•	setting out policies for government procurement, customs regulation, accounting standards and business regulation;
•	fostering a regulatory environment conducive to business and enterprise; and
•	ensuring that businesses operating within Singapore's jurisdiction are compatible with international standards and practices, in areas such as company law, accounting standards and corporate governance principles.

jobResponsibilities:
• Ensuring optimal provision, allocation and management of the agency’s budget to achieve Government and agency’s strategic objectives in a fiscally sustainable and value-for-money manner; 
• Advising and applying of internal finance policies and procedures for efficient and effective financial administration for intermediate transactions; 
• Ensuring all budgetary and financial matters are performed in line with all finance regulations and guidelines;
• Supporting the Internal Approving Authority and Tender Boards by reviewing funding proposals and tender board submissions to ensure that projects undertaken are operationally and financially viable

As an Estate Manager (EM) in the Sales Department's Planning Section, you will drive operational excellence and enhance service delivery through data-driven insights and strategic planning. Your role involves:

•	Developing and maintaining comprehensive dashboards to monitor service standards and derive business intelligence;
•	Managing data analytics and responding to stakeholder data requests with accurate, timely insights;
•	Analysing housing trends to support evidence-based planning and service improvements;
•	Creating dashboards and presenting complex data in accessible formats for various stakeholders;
•	Preparing strategic recommendations and updates for Management through reports and presentations;
•	Contributing to policy reviews and public communications through research and analysis;
•	Driving continuous improvement initiatives to strengthen data transparency, reporting accuracy, and operational accountability;
•	Supporting stakeholder engagement and public education initiatives.

During your employment, you may also be rotated to take on the role of a Customer Relations Manager (CRM), to deliver quality services to applicants and residents of HDB flats. You will be involved in administration and processing of sales applications, from registration of the application to issuing of keys, assess and respond to appeals from customers who deviate from the eligibility conditions to buy an HDB flat, and draft case reports/ submissions for management’s consideration for deserving cases. Your duties will include day-to-day liaison with appellants/flat applicants, solicitors and relevant agencies on requests for housing assistance. You will also perform the role of Duty Manager at the counters and attend to cases/issues escalated by our Customer Relations Executives. In addition, you will process Enhanced CPF Housing Grant applications from flat buyers.

The Legal Division is MHA’s legal advisor. It advises the Home Team, including its various departments (e.g., SPF, SCDF, SPS, ICA, CNB), in carrying out its public duties and functions lawfully and effectively. In so doing, the division supports the important policies and exciting operations of the Home Team.
As a Legal Counsel, you will play an active role in legislative and policy projects, legal advisory work, the review of contracts, and legal work relating to criminal law detention. You will also be conducting training in the law for officers across the various Home Team departments.
Key responsibilities:
• Advising in MHA’s legislative and policy projects, including doing legal research, and advising on regulatory regimes and operations;
• Providing timely and practical legal advice on various queries to the Home Team;
• Reviewing contract documents for MHA to ensure that they are well-drafted and protect the interests of MHA;
• Developing training materials on legal issues pertaining to MHA work and conduct legal training for officers across the Home Team; and
• Working closely with officers doing policy and operations work in order to provide legal advice.

