As Assistant Manager/Manager (Strategy Branch), you will support the strategic planning process and organisational alignment for a capable, adaptive and trusted MSF. You will collaborate closely with internal and external stakeholders to:  

• Support the development and implementation of whole-of-government approaches to workforce planning, ensuring MSF's strategies complement and enhance broader public sector initiatives; 
• Deliver inter-agency or cross-agency approaches to organisational and workforce matters, which includes identifying opportunities for resource sharing, joint capability development, and develop strategies to emerging challenges that span multiple ministries; 
• Support MSF Family’s strategic workforce planning process, which would include developing workforce strategies to address current and future organisational needs
• Identify, forward plan and prioritise organisational needs to optimise manpower resources to drive capacity and productivity; 
• Develop strategies to prevent skills obsoletion within MSF officers, and to ensure our officers are future-ready with transferrable skills beyond their current job roles to take on emerging work demands; and 
• Provide secretariat support to whole-of-government platforms, committees and/or working groups, which will offer exposure to WOG decision making processes. 

You will have a unique vantage point to gain an understanding of the breadth of MSF’s work. You will have the opportunity to regularly engage senior management, MSF Family agencies and other ministries to shape organisational priorities and foster inter-agency partnerships where useful. You will be able to build organisational development skills through organisation alignment initiatives and cross-government collaboration.  

Through the above, you will assist MSF’s leadership to steer the direction of the Ministry, influence the allocation of resources, work of the various divisions, and contribute to coordinated government-wide strategic planning efforts.

